# ==============================================================================
# MotoFolio Google Drive OAuth Configuration
# ==============================================================================
# In client-side web apps, normal users do not need an API key or Client ID.
# The app administrator/developer registers ONE free Google Cloud OAuth Web Client ID
# and puts it into config.js or index.html.
#
# Steps to get your Google OAuth Client ID (2 minutes, 100% free forever):
# 1. Open Google Cloud Console: https://console.cloud.google.com/
# 2. Create a new project (e.g., "MotoFolio") or select an existing one.
# 3. Go to "APIs & Services" > "Enabled APIs & Services" > Click "+ ENABLE APIS AND SERVICES".
# 4. Search for "Google Drive API" and click "Enable".
# 5. Go to "APIs & Services" > "OAuth consent screen":
#    - Select "External" (available to any Google account).
#    - App name: "MotoFolio"
#    - User support email: your email
#    - Developer contact email: your email
#    - Scopes: Add "../auth/drive.file" (recommended: only touches files created by the app)
#    - Click Save and Continue.
# 6. Go to "APIs & Services" > "Credentials" > Click "+ CREATE CREDENTIALS" > "OAuth client ID":
#    - Application type: "Web application"
#    - Name: "MotoFolio Web Client"
#    - Authorized JavaScript origins:
#        https://motofolio.pages.dev
#        http://localhost:8000
#        http://127.0.0.1:8000
#        (Add any custom domain you deploy to)
#    - Click "Create".
# 7. Copy the generated "Client ID" (ends in .apps.googleusercontent.com).
# 8. Paste it below and in config.js:
# ==============================================================================

GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID="YOUR_CLIENT_ID.apps.googleusercontent.com"

# Google Search Console Site Verification Token (from <meta name="google-site-verification" content="..." />)
GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=""
